 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 18:12:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 062/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-surya: add a
 dedicated MultiMedia3 front-end

Purely additive anchor front-end for the Voice Call UCM verb's
Speaker/Earpiece devices, so PipeWire could open/close a real PCM of
its own instead of either sharing MultiMedia1 with HiFi or naming the
hostless CS-Voice PCM. Confirmed the front-end enumerates correctly
(aplay -l shows MultiMedia3 at device 2, CS-Voice shifts to device 3 -
/etc/conf.d/q6voiced updated to match), but opening it fails at the
kernel level with EINVAL - it likely needs additional q6routing wiring
beyond a DT node, which this patch does not provide. Left in place
since it is inert/harmless (nothing currently references it), pending
further investigation.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi    | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
index 194a0e13d..6b6da2728 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
@@ -104,6 +104,25 @@ cpu {
 			};
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Dedicated anchor front-end for the Voice Call UCM verb's
+		 * Speaker/Earpiece devices. It carries no audio and is never
+		 * routed anywhere - its only job is to give PipeWire a real,
+		 * ordinary PCM it can open/close on its own, so it creates a
+		 * sink with switchable ports for those two devices instead of
+		 * either sharing MultiMedia1 with HiFi (which PipeWire's ACP
+		 * silently refuses to build a profile for, since MultiMedia1
+		 * has a single subdevice already claimed there) or naming the
+		 * hostless CS-Voice PCM (which makes PipeWire retry
+		 * snd_pcm_start() forever against its EINVAL).
+		 */
+		mm3-dai-link {
+			link-name = "MultiMedia3";
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA3>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		/*
 		 * Hostless front-end for CS (circuit-switched) voice calls.
 		 * Opening this PCM (via q6voiced on call start) powers up the
@@ -547,6 +566,10 @@ dai@1 {
 		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA2>;
 		direction = <Q6ASM_DAI_TX>;
 	};
+
+	dai@2 {
+		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA3>;
+	};
 };
 
 &remoteproc_adsp {
